    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive output. With a strong 73.66 efficiency score, he is our most reliable asset against Hughes, benefiting from a massive +14% park factor and a favorable platoon matchup that allows his power-speed profile to peak. **Jacob Wilson** also provides immense value at the top of the lineup (68.63); his 19% boost from facing a high-xERA arm like Kelly makes him a must-start, as he is perfectly positioned to capitalize on his elite contact skills and prime table-setting order spot. **Drake Baldwin** and **Kyle Tucker** both command top-tier confidence scores above 66, anchored by strong order placement and reliable projected xwOBA outputs despite facing respectable arms in King and Nola.\n\nStrategic roster construction today forced a difficult decision regarding **Nasim Nunez**, who sits on the bench with a 53.27 score. While his versatility and speed would typically be prioritized, he is effectively squeezed out by the efficiency of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and the high-floor production of our middle infield. **Nasim Nunez** fell short primarily due to his lower batting order assignment, which suppressed his run-scoring projection compared to the core starters. Managers should exercise caution regarding **Gunnar Henderson**; despite his talent, his 57.50 score is tempered by a -15% penalty against the left-handed Rivera, and he remains a high-risk play today. Furthermore, while **Coby Mayo** carries a solid 59.20 score, his upside is tied to potential stolen base opportunities against a slow-delivering opposing battery, making him a situational watch for managers tracking our scarce SB category.",
